WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:03.770
- New economic data paint
a grim picture of March

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.803
as the country came to a standstill.

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:09.810
Business executives tell President Trump

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:12.080
that a key component to
reopening the economy

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.603
is a lot more testing.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.060
The governor of New York says he's signing

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.290
an executive order that
will require people

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.053
to wear a face covering in public.

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:24.940
I'm Shelby Holliday, and
here are your coronavirus

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:26.913
headlines from the Wall Street Journal.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:32.280
U.S. industrial production
fell 5.4% in March.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.490
It's the biggest drop in measured factory,

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:37.873
utility, and mining production since 1942.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.230
Retail sales, which include a measure

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:43.870
of purchases at stores,
bars, and restaurants,

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:47.270
fell 8.7% in March from a month earlier.

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:49.090
It's the biggest month-over-month drop

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:51.820
since records began in 1992.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:53.530
These historic lows are the result

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:56.090
of the pandemic affecting
factories, malls,

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:58.033
restaurants, and other businesses.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:01.590
Weekly jobless numbers
will be released today,

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:03.920
and the number of Americans
seeking unemployment

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:06.853
benefits is expected
to surpass 20 million.

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:10.040
Business leaders told President Trump

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:12.140
that his administration must dramatically

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:13.950
ramp up coronavirus testing,

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:16.360
according to people
familiar with the matter.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:18.920
The executives said that
tests were necessary

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:20.900
to make Americans feel confident enough

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:22.910
to resume their normal lives.

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:24.820
A White House spokesman
declined to comment

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:25.943
on the conversation.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:29.140
Trump recently announced that executives

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:31.380
from companies like General Motors, Apple,

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:33.280
and McDonald's are all part of a new

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.403
task force to reopen the economy.

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:38.880
The president is set to
release new guidelines today

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:41.780
about restarting the country
by first opening up states

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:44.093
with the least coronavirus cases.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:46.710
It will ultimately be up to governors

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:49.680
to decide when to open their states.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:53.480
- All people in public must have a mask--

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.540
- [Shelby] In the hardest-hit U.S. state,

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.590
New York Governor Andrew Cuomo announced

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:00.410
a new face mask rule
that will kick in Friday.

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:01.950
People will be required to wear

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:03.820
face coverings in public settings,

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:06.270
where they can come into
contact with others,

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:09.613
like in grocery stores, or when
using public transportation.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:13.190
Coverings include medical masks,

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:15.413
as well as bandanas or scarves.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:18.570
Cuomo said there could
eventually be penalties

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:20.943
for people who don't
comply with the order.

